#: ../../../appimage.rst:2
msgid "AppImage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:4
msgid ""
"`AppImage <https://appimage.org/>`_ is a format for distributing portable "
"software on Linux without needing superuser permissions to install the "
"application. It tries also to allow Linux distribution-agnostic binary "
"software deployment for application developers, also called Upstream "
"packaging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:6
msgid ""
"In short the AppImage is one executable file which contains both xonsh and "
"Python. AppImage allows xonsh to be run on any AppImage supported Linux "
"distribution without installation or root access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:9
msgid "Get AppImage from Github"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:10
msgid ""
"You can get the xonsh AppImage from GitHub and run it on your Linux machine "
"without installing it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:12
msgid ""
"wget https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh/releases/latest/download/xonsh-x86_64."
"AppImage -O xonsh\n"
"chmod +x xonsh\n"
"./xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:18
msgid ""
"If you don't have Python on your host, you may want to get it from AppImage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:20
msgid ""
"./xonsh\n"
"$PATH = [f'{$APPDIR}/usr/bin'] + $PATH\n"
"python -m pip install tqdm --user  # the package will be installed to ~/."
"local/\n"
"import tqdm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:28
msgid "Extracting and running from a directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:30
msgid ""
"An AppImage can be extracted to a regular directory.  This is useful when "
"FUSE is not available (Docker containers, WSL1, older kernels) or when you "
"want to install pip packages directly into the extracted directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:34
msgid ""
"./xonsh-x86_64.AppImage --appimage-extract   # creates squashfs-root/\n"
"squashfs-root/AppRun                          # run xonsh from the extracted "
"dir"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:39
msgid ""
"The extracted ``squashfs-root/`` directory is fully self-contained.  You can "
"rename or move it anywhere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:42
msgid ""
"mv squashfs-root ~/.local/xonsh-app\n"
"~/.local/xonsh-app/AppRun"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:47
msgid ""
"To use the bundled Python directly (e.g. to install packages or run scripts):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:49
msgid ""
"export APPDIR=~/.local/xonsh-app\n"
"$APPDIR/usr/bin/python3 -m pip install tqdm --user\n"
"$APPDIR/usr/bin/python3 my_script.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:55
msgid "Or from inside the extracted xonsh session:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:57
msgid ""
"@ ~/.local/xonsh-app/AppRun\n"
"@ $PATH = [f'{$APPDIR}/usr/bin'] + $PATH\n"
"@ python --version   # bundled Python\n"
"@ xpip install rich  # install into ~/.local/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:66
msgid "Building your own xonsh AppImage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:68
msgid ""
"The best way to build xonsh AppImage in 5 minutes is to using `python-"
"appimage <https://github.com/niess/python-appimage>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../appimage.rst:70
msgid ""
"mkdir -p /tmp/build && cd /tmp/build\n"
"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh\n"
"cd xonsh/appimage\n"
"echo 'xonsh' > requirements.txt\n"
"cat pre-requirements.txt >> requirements.txt  # here you can add your "
"additional PyPi packages to pack them into AppImage\n"
"cd ..\n"
"pip install git+https://github.com/niess/python-appimage\n"
"python -m python_appimage build app ./appimage\n"
"./xonsh-x86_64.AppImage"
msgstr ""

